## Conversation
User (ultracode effort mode) reported Anthropic released Opus 4.8 with the
same REGULAR pricing as 4.7, but a reduced fast-mode tier. User's stated
premise: 4.7 fast was "6x the cost for input and output," and 4.8 fast is
"only 3x the cost." Asked to (1) analyze how the on-disk JSONL logs let us
distinguish 4.7 vs 4.8 and regular vs fast, (2) run a workflow to analyze
everything, (3) add 4.8 + 4.8 fast pricing.

CRITICAL CORRECTION mid-task: A workflow web-research agent (high confidence,
citing platform.claude.com pricing + fast-mode docs) found the real Opus 4.8
fast multiplier is 2x base ($10/$50), NOT 3x. The "3x" in press headlines
("3x cheaper fast mode" - VentureBeat/Cryptopolitan) is a REDUCTION factor:
6x / 3 = 2x. User had conflated "3x cheaper" with "3x the cost." Surfaced the
discrepancy via AskUserQuestion with two concrete pricing.go previews; user
chose 2x (per Anthropic docs). This is why the committed fast rate is $10/$50,
contradicting the user's original literal instruction.

