## Errors & Mistakes
- First jq analysis of 4.8 entries returned EMPTY. Root cause: filenames in
  ~/.claude/projects begin with "-" (e.g. -Users-abatilo-work-ml-containers/...),
  so `grep PATTERN "$f"` and `xargs cat` treated the filename as flags. Fix:
  pass `-- "$f"` or stream with `grep -rh PATTERN .` (recursive grep handles the
  paths internally). Future agents analyzing these logs MUST account for this.
- Initial premise (3x) was wrong; nearly committed 15/75. The workflow's web
  agent caught it. Lesson: verify external pricing facts, don't trust the
  stated multiplier blindly.

## Dead Ends
- service_tier as a fast/standard discriminator: dead end, it is uniformly
  "standard" for every entry including fast ones. Only usage.speed works.
- Arbiter agent committed to "3x-flat-all-fields" (following the user's literal
  instruction) but flagged 2x as RISK 1 / most-likely-correct. We overrode the
  arbiter with the web evidence after user confirmation.

## Hints for Future Agents
- To add a new model: one line in pricing.go modelPricing map keyed by the exact
  message.model string, plus a ":fast" variant. No date suffix for Opus 4.x
  (4-8/4-7/4-6 are bare; only 4-5 and Sonnet/Haiku carry date suffixes).
- Cache rates are structurally input*1.25 (5m write), input*2 (1h write),
  input*0.1 (read). A fast tier is just a scalar multiple of the regular row;
  keep all 5 fields at the same multiple or you break that invariant.
- The cache already stores the ":fast"-suffixed model string (suffix is applied
  at parse time in processFileForCache), and pricing is applied at display time,
  so pricing changes take effect WITHOUT --clear-cache. CacheVersion is 5.

## Codebase Discoveries
- opus[1m] (26 entries, 1M-context variant) has NO pricing key -> falls to
  default ($3/$15), undercharging. Bare "opus" (5) resolves to the opus key.
  Flagged to user as out-of-scope; NOT fixed in this commit. Candidate follow-up:
  add opus[1m] / opus[1m]:fast keys (and possibly a 1M-context premium tier).
- Logs also contain gpt-5.2-codex / gpt-5.5 (Codex) and <synthetic> / $DRAFTER_PATH
  noise lines; the parser's input/output==0 and empty-ID guards filter most out.

